    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0464" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363/9–2144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-21T17:00:00+03:25">September 21,
                            1944—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>698. A Russian delegation headed by Kavtaradze, Vice Commissar of Foreign
                    Affairs, with two other members and several technical experts has arrived here.
                    On September 13 they had an interview with the Prime Minister and on the 16th
                    were received by the Shah.</p>
                <p>I learned from a trustworthy official source that the purpose of this delegation
                    is to examine into the oil fields at Kavirkhourian in the region of Semnan. This
                    field has been the object of dispute and uncertainty for many years. It is,
                    however, only a small part of the northern area where oil may be expected to be
                    found. Kavtaradze has told the Prime Minister of Iran so far only that he would
                    like to make a technical examination of the fields and the Russian experts have
                    already proceeded to the spot for that purpose. The Prime Minister has said
                    confidentially to the British Ambassador that so far <pb facs="0465" n="453"
                        xml:id="pg453"/> no proposal has been made to revive the old concession
                    which was never ratified nor to make new proposals regarding oil concessions in
                    the northern region. There is no indication at present that the Russian object
                    is to block concessions in the south to either the Americans or British.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
